      "level": "nudge",
      "text": "When $x$ is huge, the $+1$ and the $-2$ are crumbs. Only the leading terms matter."
    },
    {
      "level": "guide",
      "text": "Compare the leading terms: $\\frac{3x}{x}$."
    },
    {
      "level": "reveal",
      "text": "$\\frac{3x}{x} = 3$, so the limit is $3$."
    }
  ],
  "explanation": [
    "Divide top and bottom by $x$: $\\frac{3 + \\frac{1}{x}}{1 - \\frac{2}{x}}$.",
    "As $x \\to \\infty$, both $\\frac{1}{x}$ and $\\frac{2}{x}$ go to $0$.",
    "The fraction heads to $\\frac{3}{1} = 3$."
  ],
  "alternativeExplanations": [
    {
      "title": "Plug in a big number",
      "steps": [
        "At $x = 1000$: $\\frac{3001}{998} \\approx 3.007$.",
        "At $x = 1{,}000{,}000$: $\\frac{3{,}000{,}001}{999{,}998} \\approx 3.000007$.",
        "The constants are being drowned out, and the ratio settles at $3$ — the horizontal asymptote $y = 3$."
      ]
    }
  ],
